{"ruling":{"ruling":"FULL_REFUND","amount_sgd":4.0,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"referrals":[],"confidence":0.95,"explanation":"Both sides essentially agree on what happened, and the record bears them out. To the driver: you did arrive. The trip record carries an 'arrived' event at 12:41:50, the GPS trace puts you inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE geofence from that same second (94.9 m at your nearest approach), you held position in one unbroken run of 340 seconds against the 300 second minimum, and you terminated at 12:47:30 with RIDER_UNREACHABLE, one of the codes limb (d) recognises. Taken by itself, POL-NS-01 would make the fee stand and POL-NS-07 would pay you 80% of it (SGD 3.20). The arrival marker is true, so POL-NS-05 does not re-run the clock, and the dwell exceeds the minimum, so POL-NS-06 finds no shortfall (the computed figure is a 40 second surplus, not a shortfall).

But POL-NS-01 is displaced, and the driver's own submission accepts it. POL-NS-04 is one of the clauses POL-NS-01 says displaces it, and all three of its limbs are made out. (a) The rider sent two locating/coordinating messages inside the waiting window — 12:41:05 ('im at the entrance 3 phv pickup point, which car ah?') and 12:44:40 ('boss? i still cannot see u leh') — the first delivered and read at 12:41:22, the second delivered and read at 12:44:52. (b) The chat log contains no driver message at any point and trip_record.in_app_calls is an empty array, so no reply was posted within 120 seconds and no in-app call was placed before cancellation. (c) The rider track holds 105 qualifying fixes from 12:39:40 to 12:49:10, every one of them inside the 150 m rider presence radius for this zone class — mean 21.1 m, maximum 39.9 m from the pin, a single speed of 0.0 kph. A rider who was at the pin, stationary, and messaging is exonerated by the clause designed for exactly this case, and the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full with no driver compensation.

On the remaining points the advocates raised: POL-NS-03 does not arise, because the driver was inside the arrival radius rather than stationary outside it; the rider's later narrative mentions 'Entrance 1', but the message the driver actually read 28 seconds before marking arrival named Entrance 3, and the pickup pin itself is labelled 'Jurong Point, PHV Pickup Point, Entrance 3', so there is no wrong-entrance allocation to make. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00204-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT); its absence is citable and it removes the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation route, but the driver never needed that route because his 340 second dwell is a single continuous interval. POL-GEN-01 was correctly applied by the driver: the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter is context only and was not substituted for the trailing-30-day figure, and the anti-farming test under POL-NS-07 does not trip in any event (3 terminations against a threshold of 4; rate 0.021 against 0.08) — though that check is moot once POL-NS-04 displaces the fee. Nothing in the bundle is impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d): the GPS trace is 100% coverage with no gaps, the chat log's three entries reconcile with chat_message_count, all relevant artifacts carry weight 1.0, and no POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is met. The contested SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider; the SGD 0.50 platform fee is not part of this dispute and is untouched."},"discarded_claims":[]}
